OTOGAKURE OPERATIONS — MISSION DEBRIEF
STATUS: COMPLETED
Op Ref: OP-CE-300 "Sound and Sand"

Summary
The Chunin Exam served as cover for Lord Orochimaru's infiltration of the Hidden Leaf and
for the joint operation with the Hidden Sand. Sound genin (Dosu, Zaku, Kin) entered as
sanctioned examinees to screen targets and apply pressure during the trials.

Outcomes
- Cover held through the forest and preliminary stages. Sound examinees performed as
  screen and were expendable by design.
- The alliance with Sand advanced to the operational phase per the external liaison
  agreement. Sand committed forces on the understanding of shared aims — an understanding
  Lord Orochimaru did not intend to honor beyond utility.
- Lord Orochimaru personally engaged and eliminated the Third Hokage during the assault.

Assessment
Primary objective (removal of the Third and demonstration of Sound's reach) achieved.
The operation cost the expendable genin and much of the alliance's goodwill with Sand;
both were acceptable within the plan. See the alliance postmortem held by Sand.

Filed post-operation. Retained for doctrine.
